{"version":"1","id":"developer20","handle":"developer20","name":"Developer 2.0","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/4ce9fa00296c4debace3f47acd3e3d16","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-6.5506,"y":-3.001,"cluster_id":1,"posts_collected":37,"newest_post_at":"2026-05-07T09:37:36.703Z","oldest_post_at":"2018-03-24T00:00:00.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.0,"listicle_ratio":0.0,"question_ratio":0.054054,"avg_read_time":5.135135,"summary_length_avg":256.243243,"title_length_avg":32.783784,"title_length_var":173.304602,"tag_entropy":2.359997,"tag_diversity":0.621622,"top_tag_share":0.432432,"avg_upvotes":0.621622,"median_upvotes":0.0,"avg_comments":0.054054,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.125,"zero_engagement_share":0.756757,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":0.328695,"non_article_ratio":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":0.057143},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-5.1176,5.1324],"cadence_depth":[-5.9118,-2.0882],"hype_variety":[-8.5441,-7.5],"title_style":[6.1176,-7.6176]},"top_tags":[["golang",24],["testing",5],["architecture",4],["domain-driven-design",3],["performance",2],["security",2],["kubernetes",1],["authentication",1]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["Go libs I don't use but are popular","\u00b7 Developer 2.0","How to send multiple variables via channel in golang?"],"outlier":["Deep Work: Rules for Focused Success in a Distracted World"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"wCXiTdweX","title":"How Go heap escape analysis works and how to use it","url":"https://developer20.com/notes/Heap-Escape-Analysis-in-Go","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/developer-2-0-wcxitdwex","summary":"Go's compiler performs escape analysis to determine whether variables should be allocated on the stack or heap. When the compiler cannot guarantee a variable's lifetime is bounded to the caller function, it moves the variable to the heap. Using interfaces is one common reason for heap escapes. The `-gcflags=\"-m\"` flag (or `go tool compile -m`) reveals escape analysis output, showing which variables are moved to the heap and what inlining optimizations occur \u2014 useful for diagnosing unexpected heap allocations.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--P4t4XyoV--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2001","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-07T09:37:36.703Z"},{"id":"0cMTwYBnb","title":"What I learned wiring SSO across my homelab","url":"https://developer20.com/homelab-sso-with-authentik","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/what-i-learned-wiring-sso-across-my-homelab-0cmtwybnb","summary":"A homelab engineer shares hard-won lessons from wiring Authentik SSO across Vault, Grafana, Nextcloud, Headlamp, and kubectl on a kubeadm Kubernetes cluster. Key pitfalls covered: hairpin NAT failures requiring internal DNS fixes, cert-manager HTTP-01 challenges silently expiring without port 80, Authentik's default groups scope returning empty due to a stale Django accessor (fix: use ak_groups.all() in a custom property mapping), a Grafana 11.6 regression requiring explicit groups_attribute_path, Nextcloud blocking RFC1918 addresses by default, and kube-apiserver OIDC debugging being nearly opaque at any log level. The post also documents Authentik Helm chart breaking changes (Redis removal, deprecated ingress block) and explains why Headlamp's auth model is really the apiserver's auth model. Practical Terraform snippets are included throughout.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--ZrL_HSsR--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2006","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-07T07:37:29.892Z"},{"id":"60bzn1M6e","title":"Part 1: pprof Quick Start - Get Profiling in 10 Minutes","url":"https://developer20.com/pprof-part1-quick-start/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/part-1-pprof-quick-start---get-profiling-in-10-minutes-60bzn1m6e","summary":"Learn how to use Go's built-in pprof profiling tool to identify performance bottlenecks in your applications. Covers CPU profiling to find hot functions, memory profiling to detect leaks and reduce allocations, and goroutine profiling to spot blocking issues. Includes practical examples of common performance problems like N+1 queries, unnecessary JSON marshaling, and string concatenation in loops, with concrete fixes that reduced response times from 2 seconds to 50ms.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/7ffb2836886233640cc42b6d645e1b47?_a=AQAEulh","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-12-01T07:02:59.774Z"},{"id":"gn3YJmYWj","title":"Go libs I don't use but are popular","url":"https://developer20.com/go-libs-i-dont-use/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/go-libs-i-don-t-use-but-are-popular-gn3yjmywj","summary":"The post discusses popular Go libraries that the author chooses to avoid, highlighting their drawbacks, especially in larger projects. It covers sqlmock, GORM, and gorilla mux, providing reasons like brittleness in tests, complexity in schema migrations, and performance bottlenecks. Alternative approaches such as integration testing, using sqlx, and sticking to Go\u2019s standard net/http package are suggested for more maintainable and scalable solutions.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--OHB84bZF--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2010","num_upvotes":15,"num_comments":2,"created_at":"2024-09-10T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"FAv3nKlzT","title":"Testing code with unpredictable or random output","url":"https://developer20.com/test-with-random/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/testing-code-with-unpredictable-or-random-output-fav3nklzt","summary":"Learn how to test functions in Go that involve randomness. Techniques discussed include using dependency injection, seeding random values, and statistical testing to handle unpredictable outputs while ensuring code quality and test reliability.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--VDukGCjf--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2002","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-08-12T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"2W8PXkS12","title":"\u00b7 Developer 2.0","url":"https://developer20.com/notes/Heap-Escape-Analysis-in-Go/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/developer-2-0-2w8pxks12","summary":"The Go compiler relocates variables to the heap instead of the stack if it cannot guarantee the variable won't outlive the caller function. By using the `-gcflags=\"-m\"` parameter, developers can perform heap escape analysis, receiving output that shows compile optimizations. Numerous factors, such as using interfaces, can lead to variables escaping to the heap.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--HRgLpUt6--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2003","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-07-25T07:57:25.843Z"},{"id":"YkHyhJbRA","title":"How to hash and compare passwords in Go","url":"https://developer20.com/notes/Passwords-in-Go/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-to-hash-and-compare-passwords-in-go-ykhyhjbra","summary":"Learn how to hash and compare passwords in Go using bcrypt.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/179dc324eb65abefe5dac094b9955997?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-12-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"iRxbOcgVK","title":"Flattening the Package Structure","url":"https://developer20.com/flattening-package-structure/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/flattening-the-package-structure-irxbocgvk","summary":"This post explores the journey of structuring the 'productcatalog' package, highlighting the impact of overengineering, the importance of simplicity in coding, and the benefits of outside-in testing.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/179dc324eb65abefe5dac094b9955997?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-07-16T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"gmKlitLbO","title":"Password policies","url":"https://developer20.com/password-policies/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/password-policies-gmklitlbo","summary":"This post discusses the implementation of password policies in Go, including creating an interface for policies, making them configurable using functional-style code, and handling errors. It also mentions plans to add a policy to restrict leaked passwords and the use of the haveibeenpwned API.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/179dc324eb65abefe5dac094b9955997?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-07-07T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"SpahettDB","title":"My Smart Home high-level architecture","url":"https://developer20.com/smart-home-architecture/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/my-smart-home-high-level-architecture-spahettdb","summary":"A homeowner shares their high-level architecture for creating a smart home, focusing on the core requirements, the choice of Loxone as the base system, and the use of Raspberry Pi as a hub for third-party devices.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/179dc324eb65abefe5dac094b9955997?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["jooq","metaredux","rbywkly","modernescpp","rustanalyzer"],"opposite_handles":["alexfinn","tbpn","ryolu_","kloss_xyz","felixrieseberg"],"similar":[{"id":"jooq","handle":"jooq","name":"JOOQ","is_squad":false,"x":-6.4117,"y":-3.0802,"cluster_id":1,"posts_collected":130,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/a5112f5cde344480bdfe35fb062513e0","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.379976,"median_upvotes":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.007692,"avg_read_time":4.961538,"tag_diversity":0.215385},"top_tags_preview":[["sql",92],["java",32],["microsoft-sql-server",15]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-6.2059,-4.2794],"cadence_depth":[1.1029,-2.5441],"hype_variety":[